tion Contest - 1st Prize",desc:"K. Manikandan and K. Ariharan (II - I&C) secured 1st Prize in Paper Presentation and received a cash award of ₹3,000 at KSR Polytechnic College."},{year:"2025 - 2026",title:"Outstanding Sports Achievements - Akilan S",desc:"Akilan S (II - I&C) secured State 2nd Place in 400x400 Relay and 1500m at MAM Polytechnic, Trichy. He also won Divisional 1st Place in 400x400 Relay, 2nd Place in 1500m, and 2nd Place in 10000m at Kongu Polytechnic College."},{year:"2025 - 2026",title:"State & Divisional Athletic Champion - Sakthivel L",desc:"Sakthivel L (III - I&C) secured State 1st Place in High Jump at MAM Polytechnic, Trichy. He also won Divisional 1st Place in High Jump and 1st Place in 110m Hurdles at Kongu Polytechnic College."}],labGallery:[{src:"/assets/departments/selected/ic selected/IC (1).webp",title:"Process Control Laboratory",desc:"Level, temperature, pressure, and flow control loops."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/ic selected/IC (3).webp",title:"Industrial Instrumentation Lab",desc:"Calibration of smart transmitters, gauges, and RTDs."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/ic selected/IC (4).webp",title:"Virtual Instrumentation Lab",desc:"LabVIEW data acquisition systems and virtual test benches."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/ic selected/IC (6).webp",title:"Transducers & Signal Conditioning Lab",desc:"Strain gauges, LVDT, thermocouples, and signal amplifiers."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/ic selected/IC (7).webp",title:"DCS & PLC Automation Laboratory",desc:"Distributed control systems and supervisory control."}],ivGallery:[{src:"/assets/departments/I&C/Inaugural function.webp",title:"Home Technologies Lecture",desc:"Special guest lecture on Home Technologies."},{src:"/assets/departments/I&C/Valedictory function.webp",title:"Industrial Automation Lecture",desc:"AGM of Sakthi Sugars delivering a guest lecture."},{src:"/assets/departments/I&C/Kerala Electrical & Allied Engineering.webp",title:"KEL Visit",desc:"Industrial visit to Kerala Electrical & Allied Engineering."}],events:[{date:"25 Feb 2026",title:"Guest Lecture on 'Industrial Automation'",type:"Guest Lecture",speaker:"Mr. V. Ramesh",designation:"Assistant General Manager – Co-Gen. Electrical (Head Power Plant)",organization:"Sakthi Sugars Limited, Sakthi Nagar",venue:"Dheeran Chinnamalai Seminar Hall",time:"10:30 A.M.",outcomes:["Understand the fundamentals and significance of industrial automation in modern industries.","Gain knowledge of automation components such as sensors, actuators, PLCs, and SCADA systems.","Explore the role of automation in improving productivity, efficiency, and safety.","Learn about automation practices adopted in power plants and process industries.","Develop awareness of career opportunities and emerging trends in industrial automation."]},{date:"02 Sep 2025",title:"Field Visit to TBI & IoT Labs at KEC",type:"Field Visit",venue:"TBI @ KEC and Centre of Excellence on IoT @ E&I Dept., KEC",outcomes:["Observe startup prototypes, incubation modules, and engineering innovations.","Understand sensor integrations, microcontrollers, and IoT protocols in automation.","Explore real-time data monitoring systems and calibration methods."]},{date:"07 Aug 2025",title:"Industrial Visit to Kerala Electrical & Allied Engineering",type:"Industrial Visit",venue:"Kerala Electrical & Allied Engineering Co. Ltd, Kochin",outcomes:["Understand electrical machine manufacturing and process instrumentation.","Observe transformer core assembly, coil winding, and quality testing methods.","Learn about industrial safety practices and workflow in process automation."]},{date:"18 Jul 2025",title:"Special Lecture on 'Home Technologies'",type:"Special Lecture",speaker:"Mr. P. R. Srenivasan, DECE",designation:"Managing Director",organization:"Mark Technologies & Cinespa Private Limited, Coimbatore",venue:"Kalingarayan Seminar Hall",time:"10:30 A.M.",outcomes:["Understand the fundamentals and emerging trends in home technologies.","Gain knowledge of smart home systems and automation concepts.","Explore the applications of modern technologies in residential environments.","Recognize the role of electronics and communication technologies in enhancing home safety, comfort, and energy efficiency.","Develop awareness of career opportunities and innovations in the field of home technology."]}],icon:(0,a.jsxs)("svg",{className:"w-6 h-6",fill:"none",stroke:"url(#dg-inst)",strokeWidth:"2",viewBox:"0 0 24 24",children:[(0,a.jsx)("defs",{children:(0,a.jsxs)("linearGradient",{id:"dg-inst",x1:"0%",y1:"0%",x2:"0%",y2:"100%",children:[(0,a.jsx)("stop",{offset:"0%",stopColor:"#91C04A"}),(0,a.jsx)("stop",{offset:"100%",stopColor:"#009EDB"})]})}),(0,a.jsx)("path",{strokeLinecap:"round",strokeLinejoin:"round",d:"M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2z"})]})},{id:"networking",slug:"networking",name:"Communication & Computer Networking",fullName:"Communication & Computer Networking",established:2021,intake:60,duration:"3 Years",syllabus:"/assets/departments/CCN/1055 -Communication & Computer Networking.pdf",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&q=80",slogan:"From connecting devices to connecting possibilities — we prepare students for the digital world ahead.",description:"Department of Communication and Computer Networking (CCN) was established in 2021. It has been offering quality technical education in the field of Communication and Computer Networking for past few years. Our curriculum is designed to impart both strong foundational theories and intensive practical skills in the laboratories. Students gain comprehensive hands-on operational experience with industry-standard machinery, instruments, and software systems.",overviewBullets:["The Department of Communication and Computer Networking (CCN) was established in 2021.","The department has an annual intake of 60 students.","It has been offering quality technical education in the field of Communication and Computer Networking for past few years.","The department provides knowledge in Softwares, Communication and Networking.","Students learn about: Programming languages, Artificial Intelligence, Networks, Communication systems, and Circuits.","The curriculum includes basic concepts of: Operating system, Electronics, Internet of Things, and Cloud Computing.","The department helps students develop technical and practical skills required for company."],vision:"To provide quality technical education in the field of Communication and Computer Networking, preparing students with industry-oriented expertise and strong practical skills.",mission:["To educate and prepare students in programming languages, Artificial Intelligence, networks, communication systems, and circuits.","To help students develop the technical and practical skills required for software and core companies, cloud platforms, and cybersecurity."],keyStrengths:["Experienced faculty members.","Well-equipped laboratories.","Industry-oriented learning.","Focus on practical knowledge and skill development.","Good career opportunities in the telecommunication and IT industry."],coreAreas:["Computer Networking & Data Communication","Artificial Intelligence and Intelligent Systems","Operating Systems & System Administration","Wireless & Mobile Communication","Internet of Things (IoT)","Cloud Computing & Virtualization","Programming – C, Java & Python"],learningBeyond:["Mini & Major Projects","Networking and IoT Lab Activities","Industry Visits & Internships","Industry-Linked Training Programmes (TNSDC courses)","Value-Added Certification Courses","Seminars & Technical Events"],skillDevelopment:["Network & Connectivity Skills","Cybersecurity & Digital Protection","IoT & Smart Technology","Cloud & Virtualization Skills","Programming & Software Development","Problem-Solving & Critical Thinking","Innovation & Entrepreneurship","Communication & Teamwork","Technical Troubleshooting","Industry-Ready Digital Skills"],hodMessage:"Welcome to the Department of Communication and Computer Networking (CCN) — a place where technology meets curiosity, innovation meets opportunity, and learning goes beyond the classroom. In a world driven by connectivity, our department empowers students with strong foundations in computer networking, communication technologies, cybersecurity, IoT, cloud computing, programming, and emerging digital technologies. Through hands-on learning, industry interaction, projects, and skill-based training, we nurture students to become confident problem-solvers and future-ready professionals. Our vision is not merely to teach technology, but to inspire students to understand it, build with it, secure it, and create what comes next. Let us connect knowledge with innovation and transform potential into possibilities.",labs:["Electronics Devices & Circuits Laboratory – Explore electronic components, circuits, characteristics, and practical applications.","Analog & Digital Electronics (ADE) Laboratory – Learn and experiment with analog and digital circuits, logic gates, and electronic systems.","Computer Networking Laboratory – Practical experience in network configuration, connectivity, and troubleshooting.","Computer Programming Laboratory – Develop programming, computational, and problem-solving skills.","IoT Laboratory – Build smart, connected applications using sensors, controllers, and IoT technologies.","Network Security Laboratory – Explore cyber security, network protection, and secure communication.","Cloud Computing Laboratory – Gain practical exposure to cloud platforms, virtualization, and modern computing.","Project & Innovation Laboratory – Transform ideas into working prototypes through hands-on projects and experimentation."],careers:["Jobs Opportunities in both software and core companies.","Opportunities to design secure network architectures.","Careers in the installation and maintenance of computer networks.","Employment in cloud platforms and cyber security.","Opportunities to work in India and abroad.","To become an Entrepreneur."],faculty:[{name:"Sreetharan.V",designation:"SG1-HOD",doj:"06-06-2008",dob:"21-06-1984",qualification:"M.E., MBA. (PhD).",experience:"18 Years 0 Months",phone:"9842791917",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/CCN/Sreedharan.webp"},{name:"Nancy Amala Rani.J",designation:"Lecturer",doj:"05-06-2023",dob:"25-05-1995",qualification:"B.E.,",experience:"3 Years 0 Months",phone:"9500265929",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/CCN/Nancy.webp"},{name:"Thilagaraj.K",designation:"Lecturer",doj:"05-06-2023",dob:"31-01-1991",qualification:"M.E.,",experience:"3 Years 0 Months",phone:"7502156789",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/CCN/thilakaraj.webp"},{name:"Janaki.N",designation:"Lecturer",doj:"06-07-2023",dob:"23-05-2000",qualification:"B.E.,",experience:"2 Years 11 Months",phone:"9597600671",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/CCN/Janaki.webp"},{name:"S. Poojasree",designation:"Lecturer",doj:"17-11-2025",dob:"10.06.2003",qualification:"B.Tech.",experience:"0 Years 7 Months",phone:"9500433074",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/CCN/poojasri.webp"},{name:"Manoranjitham.R",designation:"Asst. Programmer",doj:"08-09-2021",dob:"12-05-1992",qualification:"Msc., B.Ed.,",experience:"4 Years 9 Months",phone:"9944183894",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/NONTEACHING kpc/CCN/manoranjitham.webp"}],alumni:[{name:"Sridharan.P",batch:"2022 – 2025 Batch",salary:"5 Lakh/Annum",position:"Contract supervisor",company:"MRF Tyres",location:"Chennai",image:"/assets/departments/CCN/SRIDHARAN P.webp"}],achievements:[{year:"2026",title:"Divisional Chess Championship – I Prize",desc:"Our students Boopalan N and Hemachandir R won I Prize in chess in Divisional Match."},{year:"2025",title:"State-Level Paper Presentation – Cash Prize",desc:"Our students ROHIT V K, SABARINATH R, NAVEENKUMAR S, AKASH D Won cash Prize of Rs.1000 in Paper presentation held at Nandha polytechnic college, Perundurai."},{year:"2025",title:"Smart India Hackathon (Internal) – III Prize",desc:"Our students Dharun E, Yashwanth R, Vasanth K, Savitha P, Divyadharshini M, Sanjai kavin K S won III Prize in Internal Smart India Hackathon - 2025."},{year:"2025",title:"Inter-Collegiate Hockey Tournament – II Prize",desc:"Our student Sanjeev Kumar V and Ram Ratheesh K B won II Prize in HOCKEY held at KONGHU VELLALAR POLYTECHNIC COLLEGE."}],events:[{date:"20 Aug 2026",title:"Association Session on 'What Does the Industry Actually Expect?'",type:"Association Function",speaker:"Mr. Suganth Krishna Eswaramoorthy",designation:"Product Specialist",organization:"TrusTrace, Coimbatore",desc:"The Communication and Computer Networking Association organized an insightful session on 20.08.2026 on the topic “What Does the Industry Actually Expect?”. The session was led by Mr. Suganth Krishna Eswaramoorthy, Product Specialist, TrusTrace, Coimbatore, who shared valuable insights on current industry trends, technical skills, employability, and the importance of continuous learning. The session provided students with practical exposure to real-world industry expectations and motivated them to enhance their skills for future career opportunities.",outcomes:["Understand current tech industry trends and real-world employer expectations.","Gain valuable insights on core technical skills, employability, and industry readiness.","Recognize the importance of continuous learning and proactive skill development in tech careers.","Enhance career preparedness and motivation for future professional opportunities."],industryExposure:"Real-world industry benchmarks, employability standards, and skills roadmap by TrusTrace."},{date:"18-19 Aug 2026",title:"Field Trip to Kanavu Startup Village",type:"Field Trip",location:"Sivagiri",venue:"Kanavu Startup Village, Sivagiri",participants:"CCN Students and Faculty Members",desc:"The Communication and Computer Networking (CCN) Department of Kongu Polytechnic College organized a field trip to Kanavu Startup Village, Sivagiri, on 18.08.2026 and 19.08.2026. The visit introduced students to the startup environment and entrepreneurial culture, providing them with an opportunity to explore innovative ideas, understand the journey of emerging ventures, and interact with the evolving startup ecosystem. The field trip encouraged students to think creatively, explore new possibilities, and develop an interest in innovation and entrepreneurship.",outcomes:["Explore firsthand the startup environment, venture incubation, and entrepreneurial culture.","Understand the lifecycle, challenges, and milestones of emerging technology ventures.","Interact with innovative minds and observe the evolving regional startup ecosystem.","Foster creative thinking, problem-solving, and inspiration for innovation and entrepreneurship."],industryExposure:"Direct immersion into entrepreneurial culture and emerging venture ecosystems at Kanavu Startup Village."},{date:"17 Feb 2026",title:"Guest Lecture on 'Hands on AI Tools'",type:"Guest Lecture",speaker:"Mr. K. ManiPrasanth, B.E.",designation:"Managing Director",organization:"Microssoft solutions, Tirupur",venue:"Dheeran Chinnamalai Seminar Hall",time:"10:30 A.M.",outcomes:["Understand the basic concepts of Artificial Intelligence and generative AI tools.","Gain knowledge problem data privacy principles.","Analyze and evaluate the outputs generated by AI tools for accuracy and relevance.","Develop entrepreneurial and problem solving skills."]},{date:"01 Aug 2025",title:"Special Lecture on 'Recent Trends In IT'",type:"Special Lecture",speaker:"Mr. V. Gurumurthy, B.Tech.",designation:"Managing Director",organization:"Akra Group of Companies, Tirupur",venue:"Kalingarayan Seminar Hall",time:"10:00 A.M.",outcomes:["Understand the fundamentals and trends in IT.","Gain knowledge about modern IT tools and software.","Explore the innovative applications of emerging technologies.","Analyze the use of cloud based services, networking technologies and communication.","Develop awareness of career opportunities and thinking for creating technology based solutions."]}],ivGallery:[{src:"/assets/departments/CCN/Association function memento.webp",title:"Association Function - Memento Presentation",desc:"Principal Dr. V. Chandrasekaran and faculty presenting a memento to Chief Guest Mr. Suganth Krishna Eswaramoorthy, Product Specialist at TrusTrace."},{src:"/assets/departments/CCN/Association function session.webp",title:"Association Session - Industry Expectations",desc:"CCN students attending the insightful session on 'What Does the Industry Actually Expect?' in the auditorium."},{src:"/assets/departments/CCN/Association function lamp lighting.webp",title:"Association Function - Lamp Lighting",desc:"Dignitaries and faculty lighting the ceremonial lamp during the inauguration of the CCN Association Function."},{src:"/assets/departments/CCN/Field visit Kanavu Startup Village.webp",title:"Field Trip to Kanavu Startup Village",desc:"CCN students and faculty members exploring startup culture, entrepreneurship, and venture incubation at Kanavu Startup Village, Sivagiri."},{src:"/assets/departments/CCN/Field visit Kanavu Startup Village 2.webp",title:"Kanavu Startup Village Field Visit",desc:"Students exploring innovation opportunities and entrepreneurial ventures during the field visit to Kanavu Startup Village."}],labGallery:[{src:"/assets/departments/selected/CCN/ccn1.webp",title:"Network Administration & Routing Lab",desc:"Cisco routers, managed switches, and rack servers."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/CCN/CCN2.webp",title:"Network Security & Ethical Hacking Lab",desc:"Firewall configuration, VPN, and security analysis."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/CCN/CCN3.webp",title:"Cloud Infrastructure & Virtualization Lab",desc:"Virtual machines, cloud orchestration, and containerization."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/CCN/CCN4.webp",title:"Wireless & Optical Networking Lab",desc:"Wi-Fi access points, fiber optic splicing, and OTDR testing."},{src:"/assets/departments/selected/CCN/CCN5.webp",title:"Enterprise Network Systems Center",desc:"High-speed network cabling, server infrastructure, and patch panels."}],icon:(0,a.jsxs)("svg",{className:"w-6 h-6",fill:"none",stroke:"url(#dg-net)",strokeWidth:"2",viewBox:"0 0 24 24",children:[(0,a.jsx)("defs",{children:(0,a.jsxs)("linearGradient",{id:"dg-net",x1:"0%",y1:"0%",x2:"0%",y2:"100%",children:[(0,a.jsx)("stop",{offset:"0%",stopColor:"#91C04A"}),(0,a.jsx)("stop",{offset:"100%",stopColor:"#009EDB"})]})}),(0,a.jsx)("path",{strokeLinecap:"round",strokeLinejoin:"round",d:"M12 12m-9 0a9 9 0 1 0 18 0a9 9 0 1 0 -18 0 M12 3v18 M3 12h18"})]})},{id:"science",slug:"science",name:"Basic Science",fullName:"Basic Sciences",established:1983,intake:630,duration:"3 Years",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509062522246-3755977927d7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&q=80",slogan:"Foundation of engineering, catalyst of discovery.",description:"The Department of Basic Sciences serves as the crucial foundation for all students, bridging fundamental scientific principles with advanced technical disciplines. We are dedicated to cultivating analytical thinking, innovation, and a holistic approach to problem-solving. Through our experienced faculty and state-of-the-art laboratories, we ensure a seamless transition into your core professional curriculum.",overviewBullets:["The Department of Basic Sciences was established in 1983.","The department caters to all first-year students across all engineering branches with an annual intake of 630 students.","Provides absolute foundation blocks in mathematical matrix formulas, optical physics, engineering chemistry and technical English.","Staffed by experienced faculty members across Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, English and Physical Education.","State-of-the-art laboratories enable practical learning in Engineering Physics and Engineering Chemistry."],labs:["Engineering Physics Laboratory","Engineering Chemistry Laboratory","Language & Soft Skills Development Lab","Applied Mathematics Resource Center"],careers:["First-Year Academic Mentor","Technical Writer","Lab Safety Analyst","Supporting Foundation all engineering careers"],hodMessage:"Dear Students, Welcome to the Department of Basic Sciences. Our department serves as the crucial foundation for all students, bridging fundamental scientific principles with advanced technical disciplines. We are dedicated to cultivating analytical thinking, innovation, and a holistic approach to problem-solving. Through our experienced faculty and State-of-the-art laboratories, we ensure a seamless transition into your core professional Curriculum. We encourage you to approach your academic journey with curiosity and dedication. Wishing you all success in your journey of growth and development.",faculty:[{name:"Dr. Senthil Kumar S.",designation:"VP & Dept. Head",qualification:"M.Sc., M.Phil., B.Ed., Ph.D., MISTE",doj:"08.10.1994",dob:"18.01.1971",experience:"31 Years 6 Months",phone:"8778827621",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/BCS/HOD-BS.webp"},{name:"Dr. Seethalakshmi P.",designation:"SG2. Lecturer / Mathematics",qualification:"M.Sc., M.Phil., Ph.D., MISTE",doj:"14.07.2003",dob:"05.09.1971",experience:"22 Years 7 Months",phone:"9080806979",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/BCS/seethalakshmi.webp"},{name:"Ms. Rajalakshmi N.",designation:"SG1 Lecturer / English",qualification:"M.A., M.Phil., MISTE",doj:"21.06.2013",dob:"26.05.1979",experience:"12 Years 7 Months",phone:"8675114023",image:"/assets/departments/Faculty/TEACHING kpc/BCS/rajalakshmi.webp"},{name:"Ms. Hari Priya R",designation:"Lecturer / English",qualification:"M.A., B.Ed.,",doj:"18.12.2024",dob:"05.04.1998",experience:"1 Year 2 Months",